Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0008.
Per-round DSpark verify depth inside a fixed-shape verify window (VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_POLICY=conf | fixed:<d>). After each
draft, every request verifies the depth d (0..k) with the most expected tokens per ms: expected tokens = 1 + the
confidence head's prefix survivals, cost = a measured table of verify ms by live rows (VLLM_DSPARK_ROUND_MS) + the
drafter (VLLM_DSPARK_DRAFT_MS). The rule is TensorFold's V4.1 depth choice (github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold, branch
deepseek-v41-tp2, families/deepseek_v41/cuda/multi.py `_choose_k`, Apache-2.0), implemented here for vLLM's V2 runner.
vLLM's own adaptive verification refuses V4.1 (its indexer backend cannot trim verify rows); this keeps the window's
shape instead: rows past the depth are marked in is_padding, so the V4.1 router gives them top-k ids -1 and the routed
experts skip their weights, and they are invalid drafts for the rejection sampler. Rows up to the depth compute what the
full window computes for them, so greedy output does not depend on the depth. Also turns on the DSpark confidence head
when the policy is requested. Measurement knobs: VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_FILE (rank 0 reads it every 64 steps and broadcasts;
"conf:<ms by depth 0..k>" also replaces the cost table), VLLM_DSPARK_DEPTH_LOG=N (depth histogram, drafts verified /
accepted). Tests: patches/tests/test_dspark_depth_policy.py,
patches/exl3_moe/tests/test_smoe_gpu.py::test_dead_rows_leave_live_rows_bit_identical.

